Subject: [PATCH] audio: Mac ARM FFT complex multiply from the profile

Under a macOS ARM profile on a non-Mac host, the complex multiply in Web
Audio's FFT rounds the first product and fuses the second into it, as a
Mac ARM machine does. The host's vector math rounds both products
separately, so convolution and other FFT-based output differs from a Mac
in its low bits. NaN results follow the Mac ARM rules too. x86 hosts
with AVX and FMA run the same arithmetic with hardware fused
multiply-add, and other profiles keep the existing vector code.

